WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:19.759
"Oh no!" Maggie cried. "Did that van run over our bikes?"

2
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.426
"I don't think so." Cole hurried over to the bikes.

3
00:00:24.427 --> 00:00:30.019
"Here's yours, Maggie," he said, picking it up. "It looks okay."

4
00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:34.351
Henry picked up another bike. "I think they're okay.

5
00:00:34.352 --> 00:00:39.088
It looks like someone just threw them into the street behind the van."

6
00:00:39.089 --> 00:00:45.961
"Oh my!" Mr. Moss looked alarmed. "Are you sure it wasn't an accident?

7
00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:50.132
I can't imagine anyone in Belltown wanting to harm your bikes."

8
00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:54.243
Before becoming a detective, Henry couldn't have imagined it either.

9
00:00:54.244 --> 00:00:56.521
Now he wasn't so sure.

10
00:00:56.522 --> 00:01:01.928
"Did you see anything suspicious while we were inside?" he asked Mr. Moss.

11
00:01:01.929 --> 00:01:04.969
"I'm afraid not," Mr. Moss replied.

12
00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:08.240
"Shortly after you went in, I ran out of paint.

13
00:01:08.241 --> 00:01:11.709
I walked over to Belltown Hardware to buy more."

14
00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:17.346
"Maybe those little kids knocked the bikes over on their way into the Sweet Shop," Cole suggested.

15
00:01:17.347 --> 00:01:19.719
"They seemed awfully excited."

16
00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:24.268
"They might have knocked them down by accident, I guess," Maggie said.

17
00:01:24.269 --> 00:01:28.600
"But how did our bikes end up in the street behind the van?" she asked.

18
00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:31.484
"Never mind."

19
00:01:31.485 --> 00:01:36.053
Henry got on his bike and rode in a circle, testing the steering and brakes.

20
00:01:36.054 --> 00:01:38.435
Everything seemed to be working.

21
00:01:38.436 --> 00:01:42.501
"We should get going," he told Cole and Maggie.

22
00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:46.651
They said good-bye to Mr. Moss and rode toward West Belltown.

23
00:01:46.652 --> 00:01:51.423
"Do you think someone messed with our bikes on purpose?" Cole asked.

24
00:01:51.424 --> 00:01:53.794
"Maybe," Henry said.

25
00:01:53.795 --> 00:01:58.952
"Someone might be trying to send us a message to stop our investigation."

26
00:01:58.953 --> 00:02:04.775
Cole looked skeptical. "That doesn't make sense. Who would want to stop us?

27
00:02:04.776 --> 00:02:09.011
Besides, nobody even knew we were at the Sweet Shop just now!"

28
00:02:09.012 --> 00:02:12.155
"Mr. Tate did," Maggie pointed out.

29
00:02:12.156 --> 00:02:17.465
"Maybe he figured out we were getting suspicious of him and he's trying to frame Mrs. Sweet again!

30
00:02:17.466 --> 00:02:21.928
He could have followed us to town and messed with our bikes while we were in the Sweet Shop.

31
00:02:21.929 --> 00:02:26.550
Patty was too busy with those kids to look outside and notice anything.

32
00:02:26.551 --> 00:02:30.550
We were in the back of the shop, so we wouldn't have seen Mr. Tate."

33
00:02:30.551 --> 00:02:35.898
"And Mr. Moss was getting paint, so he wouldn't have seen Mr. Tate either."

34
00:02:35.899 --> 00:02:41.483
Cole looked skeptical. "Do you really think Mr. Tate did it?"

35
00:02:41.484 --> 00:02:46.982
"I guess it's possible—if he's the one who stole the flavor," Henry said.

36
00:02:46.983 --> 00:02:51.667
"We need to find out."

37
00:02:51.668 --> 00:02:55.946
When they reached the Dessert Den, an electrician's truck was parked outside.

38
00:02:55.947 --> 00:03:01.420
The electrician was inside with Mr. Tate.

39
00:03:01.421 --> 00:03:05.514
"Hi, kids," Mr. Tate said when Cole knocked on the door.

40
00:03:05.515 --> 00:03:09.103
He glanced at the electrician who was working on an overhead light.

41
00:03:09.104 --> 00:03:12.252
"I can't talk right now," he told the kids.

42
00:03:12.253 --> 00:03:15.896
"I have to make sure the lights are ready in time for my grand opening.

43
00:03:15.897 --> 00:03:17.819
Can you come back later?"

44
00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:22.566
"Sure, I guess," Cole said.

45
00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:26.878
"Now what?" Maggie said as the door shut behind them.

46
00:03:26.879 --> 00:03:31.417
They could see some neighborhood kids running around in a lot a short distance away.

47
00:03:31.418 --> 00:03:35.222
"Let's go see if Robby is over there," Cole suggested.

48
00:03:35.223 --> 00:03:43.053
"He's one of our suspects, remember?"

49
00:03:43.054 --> 00:03:46.477
"Where's Robby?" Henry asked the other kids.

50
00:03:46.478 --> 00:03:50.266
Emma shrugged. "He took off on his bike a while ago.

51
00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:52.651
I don't know where he went."

52
00:03:52.652 --> 00:03:56.858
"Have you guys seen the menu inside the Dessert Den?" Maggie blurted out.

53
00:03:56.859 --> 00:03:58.880
"When did Mr. Tate get it?"

54
00:03:58.881 --> 00:04:04.042
A kid shrugged. "I peeked in there once, but I didn't notice a sign."

55
00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:06.690
"When did you peek in?" Maggie asked.

56
00:04:06.691 --> 00:04:10.022
"Was it before or after Monday morning?"

57
00:04:10.023 --> 00:04:14.486
The kid looked surprised. "I don't remember. Why?"

58
00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:16.759
"No reason," Cole said.

59
00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:21.772
"But have any of you noticed Mr. Tate doing anything weird during the past few days?"

60
00:04:21.773 --> 00:04:26.854
"Wait," someone said. "I thought you guys were working for Mr. Tate.

61
00:04:26.855 --> 00:04:29.871
Now it sounds like you're investigating him!"

62
00:04:29.872 --> 00:04:31.947
Emma's face lit up.

63
00:04:31.948 --> 00:04:38.458
"If you're trying to prove Mr. Tate did something wrong, I bet my parents would help you! Robby's too."

64
00:04:38.459 --> 00:04:41.740
"They would? Why?" Henry asked.

65
00:04:41.741 --> 00:04:46.421
"Our parents were upset when they found out about the Dessert Den," Emma said.

66
00:04:46.422 --> 00:04:52.461
"They were getting ready to ask the town council if they could start a community garden in some of the empty lots."

67
00:04:52.462 --> 00:04:55.958
"Really?" Cole said, shooting a look at Henry.

68
00:04:55.959 --> 00:04:58.960
Henry's head was already spinning with thoughts.

69
00:04:58.961 --> 00:05:01.285
Could Emma's news be a clue?

70
00:05:01.286 --> 00:05:06.966
It sounded as if some people in the neighborhood had a motive for harming Mr. Tate's business.

71
00:05:06.967 --> 00:05:11.902
Still, Henry couldn't imagine a bunch of adults stealing an ice-cream flavor.

72
00:05:11.903 --> 00:05:15.767
Especially if they knew it would get nice Mrs. Sweet in trouble.

73
00:05:15.768 --> 00:05:21.399
"Have any of you seen Mrs. Sweet hanging around here lately?" he asked.

74
00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:27.255
Most of the kids shook their heads. But a girl named Hannah smirked.

75
00:05:27.256 --> 00:05:29.602
"Are you kidding?" she said.

76
00:05:29.603 --> 00:05:34.188
"Mrs. Sweet doesn't have time to hang around West Belltown these days.

77
00:05:34.189 --> 00:05:40.578
She's too busy going out on dates with Mr. Moss!"
